# `various` inflates a count without giving it. It often adds nothing
# (`handles various edge cases` says no more than `handles edge
# cases`), so the fix names the items, or deletes the word when the
# sentence lists them. It sits apart from the Recommended rule of the
# same name, because `various` also means `different` (`users from
# various backgrounds`), and deleting it there changes the meaning.
#
# `various` skips `different`, because the redundant-pair rule reports
# `various different`, and the filter narrows the finding back to
# `various`.
#
# It hit 119 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 18 of 20 sampled hits
# lost no meaning without `various`. Only 7 of the 18 read clearer, and
# the other 2 meant `different` (`various sizes`). The small gain keeps
# the rule Optional.
expr main [<(various !different), various>]
let message "Vague quantity. Name the items, or delete `various` when the items follow."
let description "Flags `various`, which inflates a count without giving it."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The parser handles three edge cases."
allows "The tools use various different formats."
